IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part3-div2-procedure`

-- Tests for scja1-part3-div2-procedure.l4 (ss 17B, 17C, 18). Expected values are written from the text (SCJA1969.txt lines 1236-1307), not from the code.

§ `Fixtures`

`no split of opinion` MEANS `Split of opinion` OF 0, 0

-- A hearing of a part of a civil proceeding: oral evidence in that part, and whether all the parties consent.
GIVEN oral IS A BOOLEAN
      consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Hearing
`a civil hearing` MEANS Hearing OF (Bench OF `General Division`, EMPTY), `in open court`, `a civil proceeding`, oral, consent, FALSE, `no split of opinion`

§§ `s 17B: oral hearing not needed generally`

-- (1): inputs are original civil jurisdiction, then prescribed matter
#ASSERT (`s 17B(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17B(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 17B(1) the General Division may decide the matter without hearing oral arguments` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): a part where oral evidence is given, without the consent of all the parties
#ASSERT (`s 17B(2) section 17B(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` (`a civil hearing` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 17B(2) section 17B(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` (`a civil hearing` TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17B(2) section 17B(1) allows this part of the proceeding to be conducted without an oral hearing` (`a civil hearing` FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 17B(3) the General Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17B(3) the General Division may direct that the matter be heard in an asynchronous manner by exchange of written correspondence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 17B(4) the General Division must not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17B(4) the General Division must not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 17B(5) section 17B affects the General Division's power to hear oral arguments before deciding the matter` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 17B(5) section 17B affects the General Division's power to hear oral arguments before deciding the matter` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 17C: summary dismissal of an appeal from the Registrar`

#ASSERT (`s 17C(3) the thing is an appeal for the purposes of section 17C` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17C(3) the thing is an appeal for the purposes of section 17C` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17C(3) the thing is an appeal for the purposes of section 17C` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1): inputs are the Registrar-decision condition, then limb (a), then limb (b)
#ASSERT (`s 17C(1) a Judge sitting in the General Division may on his or her own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17C(1) a Judge sitting in the General Division may on his or her own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17C(1) a Judge sitting in the General Division may on his or her own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 17C(1) a Judge sitting in the General Division may on his or her own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the opportunity to show cause and the representations
#ASSERT (`s 17C(2) the Judge may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 17C(1) now, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 17C(2) the Judge may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 17C(1) now, as the section requires` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 17C(2) the Judge may summarily dismiss the appeal under section 17C(1) now, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule for s 17B(4), run: a General Division that hears the matter asynchronously when that is inconsistent with its duty of fairness is in BREACH; one that takes some other step is FULFILLED;
-- where there is no inconsistency the rule is FULFILLED at once. (Read from the output of `l4 run`: BREACH, FULFILLED, FULFILLED.)
#TRACE `s 17B(4) the General Division shall not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 17B(4) the General Division` DOES `s 17B(4) hears the matter in an asynchronous manner` AT 0
#TRACE `s 17B(4) the General Division shall not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 17B(4) the General Division` DOES `s 17B(4) takes some other step in the matter` AT 5
#TRACE `s 17B(4) the General Division shall not hear the matter in an asynchronous manner` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 17B(4) the General Division` DOES `s 17B(4) hears the matter in an asynchronous manner` AT 0

-- The regulative rule, run. The Judge about to dismiss must give the opportunity and then consider the representations: doing both ends FULFILLED; giving the opportunity only leaves the second duty standing;
-- where the Judge is not about to dismiss, FULFILLED at once. (Read from the output of `l4 run`: FULFILLED, a residual MUST, FULFILLED.)
#TRACE `s 17C(2) the Judge must give the appellant an opportunity to show cause and consider the representations` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 17C(2) the Judge sitting in the General Division` DOES `s 17C(2) gives the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause` AT 1
    PARTY `s 17C(2) the Judge sitting in the General Division` DOES `s 17C(2) considers the representations of the appellant` AT 2
#TRACE `s 17C(2) the Judge must give the appellant an opportunity to show cause and consider the representations` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 17C(2) the Judge sitting in the General Division` DOES `s 17C(2) gives the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause` AT 1
#TRACE `s 17C(2) the Judge must give the appellant an opportunity to show cause and consider the representations` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 17C(2) the Judge sitting in the General Division` DOES `s 17C(2) considers the representations of the appellant` AT 1

§§ `s 18: powers of the General Division`

#ASSERT (`s 18(1) the General Division has the power vested in it by a written law` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18(1) the General Division has the power vested in it by a written law` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the First Schedule's answer is the seam
#ASSERT (`s 18(2) the General Division has the power set out in the First Schedule` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18(2) the General Division has the power set out in the First Schedule` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18(2) the General Division has the power set out in the First Schedule` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18(3) the power is to be exercised in accordance with the written law, Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules relating to it` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18(3) the power is to be exercised in accordance with the written law, Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules relating to it` (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18(3) the power is to be exercised in accordance with the written law, Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules relating to it` NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
